(b/'en/README.md').write_text(f'''# Reading the paper\n\n**{notice}**\n\nThis reading explains the frozen Mathesis version **2** of “{meta['title']}”. The original manuscript date is 3 November 2026; the catalog publication date is 5 November 2026. Authors, in recorded order: **Haobo Ma** (ChronoAI Pte Ltd, Singapore); **Wenlin Zhang** (National University of Singapore; ChronoAI Pte Ltd, Singapore). Paper and reading: CC-BY-4.0.\n\nThe question starts with a simple recurrence: can negative weights produce positive even rows forever? The main answer is yes for every real step at most $-3$. The manuscript also explains alternating sums and polynomial roots, including a correction to the growth scale at step $-3$. You need induction, polynomials and elementary modular arithmetic for the sign and sum chapters. The root-growth proof also uses generating functions and Rouché’s theorem; its role is introduced before the full argument.\n\nStart with Chapters 1–2 for the central sign mechanism, then Chapter 3 for row sums and root bounds. Chapter 4 explains odd-row nonvanishing; Chapter 5 separates finite root pictures from asymptotic statements. Chapter 6 records what the manuscript covers and leaves outside its scope. Every numbered manuscript theorem, lemma and corollary is retained with its complete statement and written proof. Extra introductory paragraphs explain those arguments without adding new theorems.\n\nPurple WRITTEN PROOF means that the manuscript supplies a written argument. No complete registered claim matches a frozen declaration at the current [book pin](trureturing:commit): **0 Lean-cited results, 8 written-proof results, 0 open result environments**. A nearby integer theorem is comparison context, not a verification citation for a real-parameter claim. The visualizations are illustrations; the book does not change the catalog’s verification status. This edition was written from the frozen manuscript because exact-version public Mathesis explanations are not yet available.\n\nSee [sources and provenance](source-files.md), the [coverage and limits](ch06-coverage.md), and the generated verification ledger.\n''')
